PRODID:-//Toronto Public Library — School Age//tpl.bibliocommons.com//
X-WR-CALNAME:Toronto Public Library — School Age
X-WR-TIMEZONE:America/Toronto
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Where the Lightning Has Struck: Author Talk and Craft with Pamela 
 Devonshire
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260605T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260605T150000
UID:69de66354dacf581ff88b2b8@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join Pamela Devonshire as she shares her children’s book \,\
 nWhere the Lightning Has Struck\n\, a true story about her ancestor\, Mo
 hawk Chief John Deserontyon. Pamela will talk about  why she wrote her b
 ook and why it’s important to honour and remember her ancestry. Pamela w
 ill also provide information about the Haudenosaunee Confederacy and the M
 ohawk language\, including how to say thank you in Mohawk. Children will t
 hen be invited to create their own bookmarks where they can write thank yo
 u in Mohawk (or in the language of their choice)\, while sharing their o
 wn cultures and heritage through their creation.\nDrop In. No registration
  required.\nPamela Devonshire is an author and storyteller with Mohawk and
  British ancestry. She is a proud member of the Mohawks of the Bay of Quin
 te and descendent of Chief John Deserontyon. Inspired by a passion for his
 tory and culture\, Pamela started Lightning Spark Books to share the stori
 es of significant Indigenous people\, legends and places.
LOCATION:Cedarbrae\, FCCR. First Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69de66354dacf581ff88b2b8
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to 3D Printing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260602T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260602T193000
UID:69fe44e73f8e7924031ec911@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn how 3D printers work and how you can print at the Toront
 o Public Library’s Digital Innovation Hubs. This class includes hands-on
  instruction with Prusa Slicer\, the software used to prepare your 3D obje
 ct file for printing on a Prusa MK3S+ 3D printer.\nDROP IN\nNote: Customer
 s are no longer required to attend a mandatory 3D printing class prior to 
 using a 3D printer at the Toronto Public Library’s Digital Innovation Hu
 bs. This class is for those who are interested in learning more about 3D p
 rinting and how to use the Prusa software.
LOCATION:Dufferin/St.Clair\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fe44e73f8e7924031ec911
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
