BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pawsitively Pets: Hands-on Animal Education
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260806T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260806T150000
UID:69fcdc76c7d3cd580057ab5a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Pawsitively Pets is a hands-on animal education program that o
 ffers positive animal interactions for children and adults of all ages. It
 s goal is to provide the animal team\, made up of an assortment of rescued
  pets\, with a permanent home and the best possible care while sharing a l
 ove for animals with others. All Pawsitively Pets programs focus on respon
 sible pet ownership and the lifelong commitment of owning a pet.\nAges 5 a
 nd up.\nSpace is limited. Free tickets will be distributed from the front 
 desk 30 minutes prior to the program.
LOCATION:Runnymede
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fcdc76c7d3cd580057ab5a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Story & Film: Jonathan Cleaned Up
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260625T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260625T160000
UID:6a1060ba8ea300e26317b994@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Jonathan is trying not to make a mess\, but someone has put a 
 subway station in his apartment!\nTo figure out what's going on\, Jonathan
  goes to City Hall and discovers something about the City Hall computer th
 at just might help him fix his problem.\nJoin us for a storytime with the 
 Robert Munsch story\nJonathan Cleaned Up…Then He Heard a Sound\nand a sc
 reening of the animated version from the National Film Board\,\nBlackberry
  Subway Jam\n. Drop-in.
LOCATION:Danforth/Coxwell\, 2nd Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1060ba8ea300e26317b994
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
