DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260813T173000
UID:69e8d4e68ddc1caf5f1e827d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The North York Central Library and its neighbourhood is home t
 o a variety of trees. Join the\nCity of Toronto Urban Forestry\nstaff to e
 xplore the natural world on a local neighbourhood walk. Learn how to recog
 nize different species and fun facts about their cultural and ecological i
 mportance.\nChildren under 12 must be accompanied by a parent/caregiver.\n
 Please note\, the tour will start and end at the North York Central Librar
 y\, Room 1\, and will be guided by the City of Toronto Urban Forestry staf
 f. There may be uneven\, unpaved surfaces along the route. Please dress an
 d prepare accordingly for this outdoor program (e.g. hats\, sunscreen\, wa
 ter\, comfortable shoes).\nRegistration is required.\nThis program takes p
 lace rain or shine. In the event of severe inclement weather\, you will be
  notified of an alternative date.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 1\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e8d4e68ddc1caf5f1e827d
