DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260805T150000
UID:6a037382703c336300271f93@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:For children ages 6-12 with their parent or caregiver.\nThis i
 nteractive puppet show from Chad Solomon features characters from the Rabb
 it and Bear Paws children's graphic novel series. In this performance\, au
 diences will experience the story of how the turtle carried our world on h
 er back\, and how the tiny muskrat succeeded in giving us the greatest gif
 t of all - a place to call home\, Turtle Island.\nChad Solomon is a member
  of the Henvey Inlet\, First Nation who’s grandfather taught him that no
  matter how old you become\, you should always be young-at-heart and that 
 laughter is the greatest medicine.\nNo registration – but ticket is requ
 ired. Space is limited. Large groups and daycares cannot be accommodated. 
 Tickets will be handed out at the 2nd floor desk 15 minutes before the pro
 gram starts.
