BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rainbow Sensory Storytime Social for Neurodivergent Children
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T160000
UID:69b41636b48451fc3c08a072@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a special Rainbow Storytime version of the adapt
 ed Sensory Storytimes for children aged 4-12 and their families to enjoy s
 tories\, songs\, and rhymes in a sensory-aware environment with sensory to
 ols\, toys and accessories. The storytime will include a range of inclus
 ive books\, stories\, songs and rhymes that foster acceptance\, embrace d
 iversity\, and help get kids ready for reading!\nAfterwards\, join us for 
 a 30-minute Stay and Play activity session where children can explore sens
 ory bins\, and adults can connect with other parents and caregivers\, and 
 discover helpful resources.\nThese programs are specifically designed to b
 e welcoming to neurodivergent children\, including autistic children and t
 hose with sensory processing differences. The programs will take place ins
 ide S. Walter Stewart Auditorium\, with access to the Sensory Room. This p
 rogram is a neurodivergent positive space.\nRegistrants will receive a Ven
 ue Guide describing accessibility features\, sensory accommodations\, and 
 further details a few weeks before the program.\nThis event is part of Tor
 onto Public Library's ongoing Pride series. For 2SLGBTQ+ events\, reading\
 nlists\, videos and more\, check out tpl.ca/pride.\nFor more information\,
  please call 416-396-3975 to speak with the Children’s Librarian.\nInfor
 mation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collec
 ted by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, section
 s 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event a
 nd program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the
  library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\n
 answerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Auditorium with access to the Sensory Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b41636b48451fc3c08a072
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
