 enerously supported\, in part\, by donors.\nUpcoming programs:\nMay 21:  
 LEGO World Landmarks Challenge\nRecreate famous landmarks such as the Part
 henon and Chichen Itza\, entirely out of LEGO!\nMay 28: Arts & Crafts 2 Se
 ssions:\nJUNIORS 3:45 - 4:25 PM\nfor children ages 4 -6\nSENIORS 4:30 - 5:
 15 PM\nfor children ages 7 and up\nJune 4:  Board Games:\nBring some frie
 nds or make some new ones and relax with  with some board games. Parents 
 and caregivers are welcome to play too!\nJune 11: Arts & Crafts 2 Sessions
 :\nJUNIORS 3:45 - 4:25 PM\nfor children ages 5 - 7\nSENIORS 4:30 - 5:15 PM
 \nfor children ages 8 and up\nJune 18: Robotic Fun 2 Sessions:\nJ\nUNIORS 
 3:45 - 4:25 PM\nfor children ages 6 and 7\nSENIORS 4:30 - 5:15 PM\nfor chi
 ldren ages 8 and up.\nJune 25:  Gambit the Magician:\nThis fun and entert
 aining presentation features magic tricks from each major branch of scienc
 e.
