DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260609T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260609T153000
UID:69fdddb5c6a1dc3d00d2589d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Curious about what your toys get up to when you are not lookin
 g? We jumped into the toy box to discover just that. From dolly’s advent
 ures to teddy bears on the search for honey to toy soldiers on patrol. Joi
 n us for a free guided tour of TD Gallery’s current exhibition Toys Aliv
 e! Explore literary works from the late 1800s to present day from the Osbo
 rne Collection of Early Children’s Books!\nRegistration is not required 
 but is encouraged. Please meet at the entrance to the TD Gallery.\nInforma
 tion Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collecte
 d by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 
 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and
  program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the l
 ibrary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nan
 swerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, TD Gallery\, first floor of Toronto R
 eference Library
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fdddb5c6a1dc3d00d2589d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:After School Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260615T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260615T170000
UID:6a00eb423f8e7924031ef8ac@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Looking for something to do after school? Come out to our Afte
 r School Club and learn new things\, make stuff\, meet other kids and have
  fun! For ages\n6-12.\nDiscover the magic of filmmaking in this engaging 4
 -week workshop\, designed and led by a local film expert. Participants wil
 l learn to write and create their own original animated films. In the fall
 \, the Toronto Public Library will celebrate these creations with a publi
 c festival event featuring a screening of the children’s films\, and add
 itional special activities.\nFor children 6–12 years old.\nSpace is lim
 ited.\nR\negistration is required. Commitment to all 4 sessions is require
 d.\nSnacks are offered during the After School Club for participants. Ingr
 edient lists will be available. Snacks are generously supported\, in part\
 , by donors.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on 
 this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libr
 aries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only 
 be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Ques
 tions about how the library handles your information can be directed to An
 swerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\,
  Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Morningside\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a00eb423f8e7924031ef8ac
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
