BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:P.A. Day Soccer Celebration
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260605T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260605T150000
UID:69c4217d2866a5b488445c98@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the beautiful game and global culture with a soccer 
 party! Test your knowledge of world flags and cup tournament history with 
 an interactive trivia game. Fill out your own tournament bracket with your
  winner predictions\, then take a picture in our photo booth. You can even
  try your hand at playing soccer with robots! Feel free to represent the c
 ountry you are supporting with shirts\, flags\, scarves\, homemade signs\,
  or however else you like. #FWC26 #WeAreToronto\nFor children ages 6-12. 
 Parents are welcome to stay during the program\, but please only register 
 children.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on thi
 s form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Librari
 es Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be 
 used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questio
 ns about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answe
 rline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, To
 ronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c4217d2866a5b488445c98
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Boba Drink Making Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260709T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260709T191500
UID:69c4515c5a2d780f42c4bb23@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Chef Yumiko leads a hands-on workshop to make the popular Asia
 n beverage\, Brown Sugar Oat Milk with Boba. Participants will learn to pr
 epare and use the classics ingredients including oat milk and tapioca pear
 ls to make this visually pleasing and sweet drink. Chef Yumiko will also p
 rovide a brief history of Boba and why it's so popular globally.
LOCATION:Mimico Centennial\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c4515c5a2d780f42c4bb23
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Therapy Dog Visits
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260622T163000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260622T170000
UID:69c455b181b67dfe32aef99c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for small group visits with therapy dogs. Children wil
 l have an opportunity to read\, listen to stories and engage in therapeuti
 c human-animal interaction. This free program is presented in partnership 
 with One Health Partners.\nChildren who live with a disability\, are neuro
 divergent\, or have experienced medical or other types of trauma are espec
 ially welcome. Suitable for school-aged children ages 6 and up. Siblings a
 ges 6 and up are welcome.\nThere are two 30-minute sessions available: 4-4
 :30 or 4:30-5:00. Please register for one session. Please click on the app
 ropriate program listing to register for that time. There will be limited 
 drop-in spots available on a first come\, first served basis.\nInformation
  Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by
  the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a
 )\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and pro
 gram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the libra
 ry handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswer
 line@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Sensory Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c455b181b67dfe32aef99c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
