BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:How to Write Non-fiction
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260813T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260813T150000
UID:69f0bdf6213814b1b5255053@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Writing nonfiction can be a challenge but author Erin Silver w
 ill make it fun and easy! We will discuss what nonfiction writing is\, how
  we can make it sound more like fiction\, and how to organize and write en
 gaging A+ nonfiction! Erin will share insider tips about her process\, whe
 re her ideas come from\, and will also read from her nonfiction book\,\nRu
 sh Hour: Navigating Our Global Traffic Jam\n.
LOCATION:Northern District\, Room 224
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69f0bdf6213814b1b5255053
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
