BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hands-on K'NEX 3-D Construction & Destruction Challenge
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260806T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260806T150000
UID:69f3e8ddfb87a3c2e2acfc37@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Have fun and collaborate to imagine\, design\, and construct l
 ightweight\, high‑strength 3‑D bridges using supplied K’NEX material
 s. Then evaluate the structures through controlled load testing using a sp
 ecialized “Bridge‑Crusher” rig\, which reveals each bridge’s perfo
 rmance through its strength‑to‑weight ratio.\nThrough multiple design 
 iterations\, participants observe how specific modifications influence rea
 l‑world structural strength. Gain an understanding of applied science an
 d engineering principles while building skills in teamwork\, creative prob
 lem‑solving\, and evidence‑based design.\nThis is a\nDROP-IN\nprogram.
  Tickets will  be given out\n15 minutes\nprior to the start of the progra
 m.
LOCATION:Port Union
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69f3e8ddfb87a3c2e2acfc37
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Boba Drink Making Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260723T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260723T150000
UID:69f3e99afb87a3c2e2acfc71@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this 45 minute to 1 hour workshop\, participants will learn
  how to prepare a classic black sugar milk bubble tea\, including decorati
 ng and mixing techniques\, as well as the breakdown of core ingredients. A
  classic lidded cup and straw will be provided to enjoy the Boba as you go
 !\n(*contains dairy)\nThis is a\nDrop-in\nprogram. Tickets will be given o
 ut\n15 mins\nprior to the start of the program.
LOCATION:Port Union
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69f3e99afb87a3c2e2acfc71
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Learn Magic with WonderPhil!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260722T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260722T153000
UID:6a0dba6ccaf93436005d136c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn to perform easy but amazing magic tricks to entertain fr
 iends and family! Discover the basic sleight of hand moves\, such as false
  transfers and palming\, and then learn how to apply these moves to some m
 agic routines. Make objects vanish or multiply before your audience's eyes
 !  You will also learn how to construct some DIY magic props to use in you
 r act.\nFor ages 7-12.  Registration is required.\nInformation Collection
  Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toront
 o Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\,
  and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program regist
 ration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles 
 your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca
 \n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Agincourt\, Main Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a0dba6ccaf93436005d136c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:3D Printing Demo - All Ages
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260704T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260704T153000
UID:6a0dbcc48ea300e263172d4e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Watch a 3D printer in action\, see samples\, learn how they wo
 rk\, and how you can use them at TPL's Digital Innovation Hubs.\nNote: Cus
 tomers are no longer required to attend a mandatory 3D printing class prio
 r to using a 3D printer at the Toronto Public Library’s Digital Innovati
 on Hubs. This class is for those who are interested in learning more about
  3D printing and how to use the Prusa software.\nRegistration will start 2
  weeks before this class.
LOCATION:Mount Dennis\, Room 2
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a0dbcc48ea300e263172d4e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wonder Workshop: Pollution Challenge
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260807T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260807T153000
UID:6a0dc5a20c0f2c4503faba6e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Do you ever think about the impact of one little person or one
  tiny thing on the planet? When one pollutant becomes many\, the planet hu
 rts. But when one person becomes many\, positive change can happen. In thi
 s workshop\, you will design and build your own creature or machine that w
 ill help keep our precious planet clean! Plus\, enter a prize draw for a c
 hance to win an awesome book. For kids ages 6-12.
