BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Meditative Art by Izabella Lipowski
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260601T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260630T235959
UID:6a1af88fc6a1dc3d00d72df1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of June the works of Izabella Lipowski ar
 e on display at Morningside branch\nIzabella believes that anyone has the 
 ability to make art. She believes that many times focusing on producing 
 “masterpieces” stays in the way of our creativity. For her\, non - rep
 resentational\, abstract drawing could be a way to let ourselves be curiou
 s\, spontaneous and playful. Her hope is that the viewers feel encouraged 
 to give it a try themselves.\nThis exhibit is part of\nTPL's Art Exhibit\n
 program. Toronto Public Library provides space for local artists to exhibi
 t their work at locations across the city. These exhibits aim to reflect t
 he diverse cultural interests of the city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exh
 ibit can be viewed during Morningside branch open hours. Please check the\
 nMorningside branch\npage before your visit.\nFree. All are welcome.\nImag
 e credit: Title of Piece: Together Medium (e.g. oil\, acrylic\, photograph
 y\, etc.): pens & metallic pencils Size/Dimensions: Small
LOCATION:Morningside
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1af88fc6a1dc3d00d72df1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
